@@ -662,10 +662,10 @@

 To use custom sleep images, set the sleep screen mode to **Custom**, **Cover + Custom**, or **Page Overlay**, then place images on the SD card:

-- **Multiple Images (recommended):** Create a `.sleep` directory in the root of the SD card and place any number of `.bmp` images inside. In **Page Overlay** mode, `.png` images are also supported. One image will be randomly selected each time the device sleeps. (A directory named `sleep` is also accepted as a fallback.)
-- **Single Image:** Place a file named `sleep.bmp` in the root directory. In **Page Overlay** mode, `sleep.png` is also supported. These files are used as fallbacks if no valid image is found in the `.sleep`/`sleep` directory.
-
-In **Page Overlay** mode, white BMP pixels and transparent PNG pixels let the current reader page show through; the remaining wallpaper pixels are drawn over the page. PNG wallpapers are supported only in this mode.
+- **Multiple Images (recommended):** Create a `.sleep` directory in the root of the SD card and place BMP, PNG, JPEG (`.jpg` or `.jpeg`), or GIF images inside for **Custom** and **Cover + Custom** modes. GIFs display their first frame only (up to 480 pixels wide on the device). **Page Overlay** mode supports BMP and PNG. One image will be randomly selected each time the device sleeps. (A directory named `sleep` is also accepted as a fallback.)
+- **Single Image:** In **Custom** mode, place `sleep.bmp`, `sleep.png`, `sleep.jpg`, `sleep.jpeg`, or `sleep.gif` in the root directory. **Page Overlay** supports `sleep.bmp` and `sleep.png`. These files are used as fallbacks if no valid image is found in the `.sleep`/`sleep` directory.
+
+In **Page Overlay** mode, white BMP pixels and transparent PNG pixels let the current reader page show through; the remaining wallpaper pixels are drawn over the page.

 > [!TIP]
 > For best results:
